# sha256 of every config netmon has shipped (configs/<site>.toml, and
# config.toml.example before it). An installed config matching one of these
# was never edited on the host, so an upgrade may replace it with the
# current one. Add the old hash here whenever a shipped config changes.
#
# As deployed to hosts. These copies held the hosts' tailnet addresses,
# which the public history replaces, so they hash differently from it.
